-- title:
--   Corollary 3.6 — the discretised kernel, two-sided and uniform in the spacing
-- statement:
--   For $d \ge 2$, $0 < \vartheta \le \pi/2$ and $0 < \alpha \le 2$ there is an
--   angle $\theta' \in (0,\pi/2]$ such that for every $\Lambda \ge 1$ there is a
--   constant $C > 0$ such that: for every $\vartheta$-bounded $\Gamma$ satisfying
--   `CondMeas`, every kernel $k$ with the bounds (2), and **every spacing
--   $h > 0$**, there is a configuration $\Gamma'$ whose apex angle is
--   *identically* $\theta'$, with, for all $x,y \in h\mathbb{Z}^d$ separated by
--   more than $\sqrt d\,h$,
--
--   $$\frac{1}{C}\Bigl(\mathbf 1[y \in V^{\Gamma'}\![x]] + \mathbf 1[x \in V^{\Gamma'}\![y]]\Bigr)\|x-y\|^{-d-\alpha}
--   \;\le\;
--   \frac{1}{h^{2d}}\!\!\int_{Q_h(x)\times Q_h(y)}\!\! k
--   \;\le\; C\,\|x-y\|^{-d-\alpha}.$$
--
--   The middle quantity is the **average** of $k$ over the two open cubes of side
--   $h$ at the two lattice points.
--
--   **$C$ does not depend on $h$** — one constant serves every spacing at once, and
--   $\theta'$ does not depend on $\Lambda$ either. That is what makes this the
--   rescaled, uniform form. $\Gamma'$ is chosen after $h$, so the auxiliary cone
--   field may vary with the spacing, but is fixed before $x$ and $y$.
--
--   The separation threshold $\sqrt d\,h$ is exactly the Euclidean diameter of a
--   cube of side $h$, so the two cubes are disjoint; nearest neighbours and the
--   diagonal are excluded outright. As in milestone 7, $\alpha \le 2$ is
--   non-strict. The apex of $\Gamma'$ is an **equality**, not a lower bound, though
--   its axis is an arbitrary unit field; and the upper bound does not mention
--   $\Gamma'$ at all. Nothing relates $\Gamma'$ to $\Gamma$, and no measurability
--   of $k$ is assumed.
